-- title:
--   Coefficients of Γ₁(Mp)-invariant functions at γ∞ lie in ℚ(ζₚ)
-- statement:
--   Let $M \ge 1$ and let $p$ be a prime with $p \nmid M$, let $m$ be a natural number, and let $G \colon \mathcal{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be a function on the upper half-plane which is holomorphic, in the sense of being differentiable for the complex model with respect to the charts of $\mathcal{H}$. Assume: $G(g \cdot \tau) = G(\tau)$ for every $g \in \Gamma_1(Mp)$ and every $\tau \in \mathcal{H}$; for every $\alpha \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ the product of $\tau \mapsto G(\alpha \cdot \tau)$ with $\Delta^m$, where $\Delta$ is the modular discriminant `ModularForm.discriminant`, is bounded as $\operatorname{Im}\tau \to \infty$; and every coefficient of the $q$-expansion of period $1$ of $G \cdot \Delta^m$ is a rational number, i.e. for each $n$ there is $r \in \mathbb{Q}$ with that coefficient equal to the image of $r$ in $\mathbb{C}$. Let $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lie in $\Gamma_0(M)$ and satisfy $p \mid \gamma_{1,1}$, the lower right entry of $\gamma$, and let $n$ be a natural number. Then the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of period $p$ of the function $(\tau \mapsto G(\gamma \cdot \tau)) \cdot \Delta^m$ lies in the subfield $\mathbb{Q}\bigl(e^{2\pi i/p}\bigr)$ of $\mathbb{C}$, presented as the intermediate field of $\mathbb{C}/\mathbb{Q}$ generated by $\exp(2\pi i/p)$.
--
--   This is the function-theoretic core of the statement that the Atkin–Lehner involution $w_{\zeta_p}$ of $X_1(Mp)$ is defined over $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ (Shimura, Prop. 6.9 and its proof): a $\Gamma_1(Mp)$-invariant function with rational expansion at $\infty$ acquires, after translation by $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M)$ with $p \mid d$, an expansion of period $p$ with coefficients in $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$. It is used in the project's rationality statements for $q$-expansions of Atkin–Lehner slashes at level $Mp$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_qExpansion_coeff_comp_smul_mem_adjoin_exp_of_gamma1_mul.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
